WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.748 --> 00:00:08.409
This gallery collects scholar media for the course: the researchers you are reading, speaking for themselves.

2
00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:16.381
Filter by week or by format. Each card names the scholar, what the item explains, and what to watch or listen for.

3
00:00:16.381 --> 00:00:27.387
Play inside the page where you can. Embeddable videos use official platform players, and nothing loads until you press play. Podcasts and restricted media link out to the official source.

4
00:00:27.387 --> 00:00:36.412
Watch or listen, then read. A talk is a way into a source, not a replacement for it. Each card names the reading move to make next.

5
00:00:36.412 --> 00:00:45.748
Write the Reading Rescue note. After the media, write one sentence you can prove from the reading. It becomes part of your weekly notes.

6
00:00:45.748 --> 00:00:48.884
Watching is never tracked or graded.

7
00:00:48.884 --> 00:00:54.313
Where next: Open the reading the media connects to in Readings and Media.
